# Hosted project link. This file is an example. Do not commit a filled-in ref if you prefer to keep it off GitHub.
#
# 1. Create a project at https://supabase.com/dashboard
# 2. Copy the project ref from the dashboard URL:
#      https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/YOUR_PROJECT_REF
# 3. From the repo root:
#      supabase login
#      supabase link --project-ref YOUR_PROJECT_REF
#      supabase db push
#
# Auth → URL configuration on the hosted project must allow:
#   heft://auth/callback
#   the admin site URL (for example https://YOUR_ADMIN_HOST)
#
# Edge function secrets (set in the dashboard or CLI, never in git):
#   supabase secrets set STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=... STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=... GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=...
# Leave them unset to keep the sandbox adapters.
